ing-view2-after_watermarked.jpg?v=1795440542","beforeThumb":"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/11\/cryo-sculpting-view2-before_watermarked-768x768.jpg?v=1795440542","afterThumb":"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/11\/cryo-sculpting-view2-after_watermarked-768x768.jpg?v=1795440542","beforeAlt":"Before: Cryo Sculpting, front view","afterAlt":"After: Cryo Sculpting, front view","description":"Front view"}],"total_pairs":2,"gender":"Male","age":"46-60","age_group":"46-60","recovery":"Minimal (1-3 days)","duration":"Single Session","results":"Immediate","procedure":"Minimally Invasive","procedure_info":"<ol>\n \t<li><strong>Consultation<\/strong>\n<ul>\n \t<li>A qualified provider will assess your goals, target areas, and suitability for Cryo Sculpting.<\/li>\n \t<li>Ideal candidates are close to their ideal weight with localized fat pockets.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n \t<li><strong>Preparation<\/strong>\n<ul>\n \t<li>The treatment area is cleaned and marked.<\/li>\n \t<li>A protective gel pad is placed on the skin to prevent frostbite or irritation.<\/li>\n \t<li>The applicator is positioned on the area and suction is applied to pull the fat into the cooling chamber.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n \t<li><strong>Cooling Process<\/strong>\n<ul>\n \t<li>Controlled cooling is delivered to the fat cells for approximately 35 to 60 minutes per area.<\/li>\n \t<li>You may feel intense cold, pulling, or tingling initially\u2014this usually fades as the area becomes numb.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n \t<li><strong>Post-Treatment Massage<\/strong>\n<ul>\n \t<li>After the applicator is removed, the area may be massaged for a few minutes to enhance fat breakdown and circulation.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<\/ol>","featured":false,"date":"May 6, 2025","timestamp":1746532740,"category":"body","categoryName":"Body","categoryNames":["Body","Body contouring"],"beforeImg":"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/11\/cryo-sculpting-before_watermarked.jpg?v=1795440540","afterImg":"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/11\/cryo-sculpting-after_watermarked.jpg?v=1795440541","beforeThumb":"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/11\/cryo-sculpting-before_watermarked-768x768.jpg?v=1795440540","afterThumb":"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/11\/cryo-sculpting-after_watermarked-768x768.jpg?v=1795440541","beforeAlt":"Before: Cryo Sculpting","afterAlt":"After: Cryo Sculpting","imagePairs":[{"beforeImg":"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/11\/cryo-sculpting-view2-before_watermarked.jpg?v=1795440542","afterImg":"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/11\/cryo-sculpting-view2-after_watermarked.jpg?v=1795440542","beforeThumb":"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/11\/cryo-sculpting-view2-before_watermarked-768x768.jpg?v=1795440542","afterThumb":"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/11\/cryo-sculpting-view2-after_watermarked-768x768.jpg?v=1795440542","beforeAlt":"Before: Cryo Sculpting, front view","afterAlt":"After: Cryo Sculpting, front view","description":"Front view"}],"ageGroup":"46-60","procedureType":"Minimally Invasive","description":"<p><strong>Cryo Sculpting<\/strong> is a non-invasive body contouring treatment designed to reduce stubborn fat by using controlled cooling technology. Also known as <strong>cryolipolysis<\/strong>, this procedure targets and freezes fat cells beneath the skin without damaging surrounding tissues. Over the following weeks, the frozen fat cells are naturally eliminated by the body, resulting in a slimmer, more sculpted appearance.<\/p>\n<p>It\u2019s ideal for individuals who are near their ideal weight but struggle with localized fat deposits in areas like the <strong>abdomen, flanks (love handles), thighs, back, upper arms, or under the chin<\/strong>. Cryo Sculpting requires no surgery, no needles, and no downtime, making it a popular choice for safe and effective fat reduction.<\/p>\n","content":"<p><strong>Cryo Sculpting<\/strong> is a non-invasive body contouring treatment designed to reduce stubborn fat by using controlled cooling technology. Also known as <strong>cryolipolysis<\/strong>, this procedure targets and freezes fat cells beneath the skin without damaging surrounding tissues. Over the following weeks, the frozen fat cells are naturally eliminated by the body, resulting in a slimmer, more sculpted appearance.<\/p>\n<p>It\u2019s ideal for individuals who are near their ideal weight but struggle with localized fat deposits in areas like the <strong>abdomen, flanks (love handles), thighs, back, upper arms, or under the chin<\/strong>. Cryo Sculpting requires no surgery, no needles, and no downtime, making it a popular choice for safe and effective fat reduction.<\/p>\n","procedureInfo":"<ol>\n<li><strong>Consultation<\/strong>\n<ul>\n<li>A qualified provider will assess your goals, target areas, and suitability for Cryo Sculpting.<\/li>\n<li>Ideal candidates are close to their ideal weight with localized fat pockets.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<li><strong>Preparation<\/strong>\n<ul>\n<li>The treatment area is cleaned and marked.<\/li>\n<li>A protective gel pad is placed on the skin to prevent frostbite or irritation.<\/li>\n<li>The applicator is positioned on the area and suction is applied to pull the fat into the cooling chamber.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<li><strong>Cooling Process<\/strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Controlled cooling is delivered to the fat cells for approximately 35 to 60 minutes per area.<\/li>\n<li>You may feel intense cold, pulling, or tingling initially\u2014this usually fades as the area becomes numb.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<li><strong>Post-Treatment Massage<\/strong>\n<ul>\n<li>After the applicator is removed, the area may be massaged for a few minutes to enhance fat breakdown and circulation.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n","doctor":{"id":20,"name":"Dr. Daniel Okafor","slug":"daniel-okafor","photo":"","photoAlt":"Dr. Daniel Okafor","credentials":"MD \u00b7 Hair restoration and weight management","location":"Westside Clinic","url":""},"doctors":[{"id":20,"name":"Dr. Daniel Okafor","slug":"daniel-okafor","photo":"","photoAlt":"Dr. Daniel Okafor","credentials":"MD \u00b7 Hair restoration and weight management","location":"Westside Clinic","url":""}],"proFilters":{"gender":"Male","age":"46-60","recovery":"Minimal (1-3 days)","duration":"Single Session","results":"Immediate","procedure":"Minimally Invasive"},"timeline":[],"journey":{"treatmentDate":"","stages":[]},"collections":[]},{"id":80,"title":"Skin Biopsy","categories":[{"id":4,"slug":"skin-care","name":"Skin care"}],"category_names":["Skin care"],"primary_category":{"id":4,"slug":"skin-care","name":"Skin care"},"main_before_image":"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/11\/skin-biopsy-before_watermarked.jpg?v=1795440543","main_after_image":"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/11\/skin-biopsy-after_watermarked.jpg?v=1795440544","main_before_alt":"Before: Skin Biopsy","main_after_alt":"After: Skin Biopsy","main_description":"","image_pairs":[],"total_pairs":1,"gender":"Female","age":"18-30","age_group":"18-30","recovery":"Minimal (1-3 days)","duration":"Single Session","results":"Immediate","procedure":"Minimally Invasive","procedure_info":"<strong>Preparation<\/strong>:\n<ul>\n \t<li>The area to be biopsied will be cleansed with an antiseptic.<\/li>\n \t<li>Local anesthesia (typically lidocaine) is injected to numb the site, so you won\u2019t feel pain during the procedure.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<strong>Biopsy Technique<\/strong> <em>(chosen based on lesion type and location)<\/em>:\n<ul>\n \t<li><strong>Shave Biopsy<\/strong>: A thin layer of the lesion is shaved off with a scalpel.<\/li>\n \t<li><strong>Punch Biopsy<\/strong>: A small, circular tool is used to remove a core of skin, including deeper layers.<\/li>\n \t<li><strong>Excisional Biopsy<\/strong>: The entire lesion is removed with a scalpel, often requiring stitches.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<strong>Duration<\/strong>:\n<ul>\n \t<li>The procedure typically takes <strong>15 to 30 minutes<\/strong>, including preparation and dressing.<\/li>\n<\/ul>","featured":false,"date":"May 6, 2025","timestamp":1746532680,"category":"skin-care","categoryName":"Skin care","categoryNames":["Skin care"],"beforeImg":"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/11\/skin-biopsy-before_watermarked.jpg?v=1795440543","afterImg":"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/11\/skin-biopsy-after_watermarked.jpg?v=1795440544","beforeThumb":"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/11\/skin-biopsy-before_watermarked-768x768.jpg?v=1795440543","afterThumb":"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/11\/skin-biopsy-after_watermarked-768x768.jpg?v=1795440544","beforeAlt":"Before: Skin Biopsy","afterAlt":"After: Skin Biopsy","imagePairs":[],"ageGroup":"18-30","procedureType":"Minimally Invasive","description":"<p>A <strong>skin biopsy<\/strong> is a minor procedure in which a small sample of skin is removed and sent to a laboratory for microscopic examination. It is commonly performed to diagnose or rule out skin conditions such as <strong>skin cancer<\/strong>, <strong>inflammatory skin disorders<\/strong>, <strong>infections<\/strong>, or <strong>unusual growths<\/strong>. Depending on the lesion and location, your dermatologist may use different techniques like <strong>shave biopsy<\/strong>, <strong>punch biopsy<\/strong>, or <strong>excisional biopsy<\/strong>. The procedure is typically quick, done under local anesthesia, and involves minimal discomfort with little to no downtime.<\/p>\n","content":"<p>A <strong>skin biopsy<\/strong> is a minor procedure in which a small sample of skin is removed and sent to a laboratory for microscopic examination. It is commonly performed to diagnose or rule out skin conditions such as <strong>skin cancer<\/strong>, <strong>inflammatory skin disorders<\/strong>, <strong>infections<\/strong>, or <strong>unusual growths<\/strong>. Depending on the lesion and location, your dermatologist may use different techniques like <strong>shave biopsy<\/strong>, <strong>punch biopsy<\/strong>, or <strong>excisional biopsy<\/strong>. The procedure is typically quick, done under local anesthesia, and involves minimal discomfort with little to no downtime.<\/p>\n","procedureInfo":"<p><strong>Preparation<\/strong>:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>The area to be biopsied will be cleansed with an antiseptic.<\/li>\n<li>Local anesthesia (typically lidocaine) is injected to numb the site, so you won\u2019t feel pain during the procedure.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Biopsy Technique<\/strong> <em>(chosen based on lesion type and location)<\/em>:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Shave Biopsy<\/strong>: A thin layer of the lesion is shaved off with a scalpel.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Punch Biopsy<\/strong>: A small, circular tool is used to remove a core of skin, including deeper layers.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Excisional Biopsy<\/strong>: The entire lesion is removed with a scalpel, often requiring stitches.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Duration<\/strong>:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>The procedure typically takes <strong>15 to 30 minutes<\/strong>, including preparation and dressing.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n","doctor":{"id":17,"name":"Dr. Amelia Hart","slug":"amelia-hart","photo":"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/11\/doctor-amelia-hart-150x150.png","photoAlt":"Dr. Amelia Hart","credentials":"MD, FAAD \u00b7 Dermatologist","location":"Harbour Street Clinic","url":""},"doctors":[{"id":17,"name":"Dr. Amelia Hart","slug":"amelia-hart","photo":"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/11\/doctor-amelia-hart-150x150.png","photoAlt":"Dr. Amelia Hart","credentials":"MD, FAAD \u00b7 Dermatologist","location":"Harbour Street Clinic","url":""}],"proFilters":{"gender":"Female","age":"18-30","recovery":"Minimal (1-3 days)","duration":"Single Session","results":"Immediate","procedure":"Minimally Invasive"},"timeline":[],"journey":{"treatmentDate":"","stages":[]},"collections":[]},{"id":83,"title":"CoolSculpting","categories":[{"id":13,"slug":"body","name":"Body"},{"id":14,"slug":"body-contouring","name":"Body contouring"}],"category_names":["Body","Body contouring"],"primary_category":{"id":13,"slug":"body","name":"Body"},"main_before_image":"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/11\/coolsculpting-before_watermarked.jpg?v=1795440